    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0179" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg83"/>

                <head>No. 51.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Fish to Mr. Partridge.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1871-11-10"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 10,
                        1871</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 22.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 16, of the 29th of
                    September last, in relation to the passage of a “law of freedom” in Brazil, has
                    been received.</p>
                <p>You will inform the government of Brazil that the President has <pb facs="0180"
                        n="84" xml:id="pg84"/> received with, much satisfaction the intelligence of
                    the passage of the law adverted to. Your course in regard to the matter is
                    approved.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>HAMILTON FISH.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
